WEBVTT

00:01.835 --> 00:05.422
KANAGAWA DISTRICT SATOZAKURA HIGH SCHOOL

00:05.505 --> 00:08.425
AUDIO-VISUAL CLUB

00:09.009 --> 00:12.554
Wait, there are five sequels
to The Super Scream Project?

00:13.138 --> 00:14.556
There are seven of them.

00:14.639 --> 00:18.810
Really? I think the seventh installation
of this series will be shocking.

00:18.893 --> 00:22.021
The seventh installation feels
totally different.

00:22.105 --> 00:24.065
It's not even a movie parody.

00:24.566 --> 00:26.192
Then what movie is that?

00:26.276 --> 00:27.527
Well…

00:27.610 --> 00:29.320
A sloppy sitcom

00:29.404 --> 00:31.406
plus family horror, I guess?

00:31.489 --> 00:32.699
What does that mean?

00:32.782 --> 00:34.784
The grandson of the owner
in the first movie,

00:34.868 --> 00:37.078
the grandson of the prisoner
in the second movie,

00:37.162 --> 00:41.666
and the grandson of the first person
who died in the third movie lived together

00:41.750 --> 00:43.209
for some reason.

00:43.293 --> 00:45.003
The house turned out to be haunted,

00:45.086 --> 00:47.714
so they invited a psychic to the house.

00:47.797 --> 00:49.716
It sounds boring.

00:49.799 --> 00:51.968
It's boring to death.

00:52.051 --> 00:53.845
Who would want to see this?

00:53.928 --> 00:57.557
But what's interesting is that
the ones in the fifth and sixth movies--

00:58.183 --> 00:59.350
What?

00:59.434 --> 01:01.102
Why are you here?

01:01.186 --> 01:05.607
Didn't we tell you not to use it
since we're using it as our club room?

01:05.690 --> 01:06.941
But…

01:07.567 --> 01:11.321
You haven't used it lately,
I thought you don't need it anymore.

01:16.159 --> 01:17.160
So?

01:18.161 --> 01:19.788
No, I mean…

01:21.414 --> 01:24.959
Just get out of here, you cockroaches!

01:25.710 --> 01:27.545
Let's go, Yoshino.

01:30.715 --> 01:33.301
Things won't end so easily
if you use this room again.

01:33.802 --> 01:35.261
Got it.

01:35.345 --> 01:37.722
Hey, what are you doing?

01:40.725 --> 01:42.227
What?

01:43.102 --> 01:44.729
I'm taking it back.

01:45.814 --> 01:46.856
What?

01:55.323 --> 01:57.617
Move your foot.

02:00.620 --> 02:03.164
Hey, stop that!

02:04.290 --> 02:06.167
I'm taking this back.

02:06.251 --> 02:07.877
Can you move your foot?

02:18.763 --> 02:20.932
-Oh, no!
-Oh, no!

02:29.315 --> 02:30.608
Close the door.

02:31.109 --> 02:32.318
Got it.

02:44.247 --> 02:46.291
AUDIO-VISUAL CLUB

02:46.374 --> 02:50.336
-Come on, stand up!
-Take this!

04:31.604 --> 04:35.316
"The antonym of like is indifference."

04:36.109 --> 04:38.569
Did the person
who came up with this go to hell?

04:39.904 --> 04:42.740
Getting along with others
with bad intentions

04:43.408 --> 04:45.827
is better than leaving them alone?

04:45.910 --> 04:47.036
That's impossible.

04:48.371 --> 04:50.623
"The antonym of like is hate."

04:51.499 --> 04:53.418
That's what Japanese people like.

04:54.085 --> 04:57.880
They complicate things
and gain joy from them.

04:58.715 --> 05:01.217
But Japanese people
didn't come up with that.

05:02.802 --> 05:05.263
I'm talking about
the fallacious statement.

05:05.346 --> 05:06.431
What?

05:07.015 --> 05:10.685
Some foreigner initially said that…

05:11.311 --> 05:14.439
"The antonym of love
is indifference," right?

05:15.857 --> 05:18.568
There are many definitions of love.

05:18.651 --> 05:22.238
That's why we can define
the antonym as "indifference."

05:22.322 --> 05:23.656
I guess so.

05:24.657 --> 05:27.952
But the Japanese
don't usually use the word "love."

05:28.828 --> 05:30.330
So in this country,

05:30.413 --> 05:33.541
it changed to "like" at some point.

05:33.624 --> 05:38.046
Can the antonyms of "love"
and "indifference" be established?

05:38.629 --> 05:41.340
No one really thought about it
before spreading it.

05:42.467 --> 05:45.178
Everyone likes to play word games.

05:45.762 --> 05:50.475
Because humans can't live
without making excuses.

05:55.980 --> 05:57.148
What's this?

05:59.484 --> 06:03.029
An experiment to test
how big can humans become.

06:05.990 --> 06:10.078
And what you're holding is a test
to see how small it can go.

06:11.537 --> 06:12.872
This is…

06:14.373 --> 06:15.708
a human?

06:18.002 --> 06:20.838
Junpei, are you used to seeing corpses?

06:21.339 --> 06:22.507
I don't know.

06:23.508 --> 06:25.426
If this were my mother,

06:25.510 --> 06:29.639
I might collapse and hate you.

06:30.765 --> 06:34.435
But I know humanity is ugly.

06:35.770 --> 06:39.398
So I don't have any expectations
for other people.

06:40.274 --> 06:43.903
I don't have any thoughts
about someone else's death either.

06:45.029 --> 06:49.784
Indifference is the virtue
that mankind deserves.

06:52.120 --> 06:55.289
And someone like you seeks revenge?

06:56.165 --> 06:59.627
Are you saying that
I'm contradicting myself?

07:01.963 --> 07:04.507
Do you think people have a heart?

07:05.007 --> 07:06.134
What?

07:06.217 --> 07:07.677
Is the answer "no"?

07:08.302 --> 07:09.971
That's right. It's "no."

07:11.097 --> 07:12.723
Humans have souls.

07:12.807 --> 07:14.725
But that's not the heart.

07:14.809 --> 07:16.978
Then my…

07:17.895 --> 07:22.066
I'm the only one in the world
who understands the structure of a soul.

07:23.776 --> 07:27.822
Because I change the shape
of a creature by touching the soul.

07:28.531 --> 07:32.702
Emotions are products
of the soul's metabolism.

07:33.619 --> 07:36.289
It's too mechanical to call it a heart.

07:37.373 --> 07:41.002
People think too much
about the things they can't see.

07:41.669 --> 07:43.504
As someone who can see them,

07:43.588 --> 07:47.383
souls are the same as bodies,
it's nothing special.

07:49.802 --> 07:51.762
It just exists there.

07:52.388 --> 07:56.184
Do you understand?
Life has no value or weight.

07:56.684 --> 07:59.312
It's like the flow of water
between heaven and earth.

07:59.395 --> 08:01.981
Life is just a cycle.

08:03.065 --> 08:07.987
You and I are the same,
meaningless and worthless.

08:10.114 --> 08:11.991
Father…

08:12.074 --> 08:14.619
Because of this,
you can do whatever you want.

08:14.702 --> 08:16.662
It's your freedom on how to survive.

08:17.330 --> 08:20.374
Don't be imprisoned by
the ideal of indifference.

08:20.875 --> 08:23.628
There's no need to implement
a single living method.

08:24.253 --> 08:28.090
Eat when you're hungry,
kill when you hate.

08:29.634 --> 08:32.803
I acknowledge
your entire existence, Junpei.

08:54.700 --> 08:55.701
I found him.

08:56.202 --> 08:58.204
Wait, casual clothes?

08:58.287 --> 09:01.624
He hasn't been to school lately.

09:03.334 --> 09:05.920
But I'm the same, too.

09:06.420 --> 09:08.464
Are the others doing well?

09:13.219 --> 09:15.888
They seem to be doing well.

09:17.431 --> 09:19.267
So what are we going to do?

09:19.976 --> 09:21.352
Use that.

09:21.435 --> 09:22.270
What?

09:22.353 --> 09:23.479
Is that a Cursed Spirit?

09:24.689 --> 09:28.651
It's a Fly Head,
a low-level Cursed Spirit below Grade 4.

09:30.403 --> 09:34.115
Once you see no one around,
use the Fly Head to attack him.

09:34.198 --> 09:35.032
What?

09:35.616 --> 09:38.995
One, if he's a normal person
who can't see the curse…

09:40.705 --> 09:43.291
Please save him.

09:43.374 --> 09:47.712
Two, if he can see the curse,
but he doesn't know how to handle it…

09:48.379 --> 09:51.382
Please save him too.

09:51.465 --> 09:54.051
Then question him about the incident.

09:54.135 --> 09:57.471
Three, if he eliminates the Fly Head
with cursed technique…

09:59.140 --> 10:00.808
Arrest him on the spot.

10:00.891 --> 10:02.476
With force?

10:02.560 --> 10:03.936
Yes.

10:04.437 --> 10:07.773
Doesn't matter if it's a misunderstanding.
We'll apologize later.

10:08.274 --> 10:09.567
However…

10:09.650 --> 10:14.947
Four, if he has the potential of
a Grade 2 Jujutsu Sorcerer and above…

10:15.489 --> 10:18.409
We'll retreat temporarily
and meet with Mr. Nanami.

10:18.909 --> 10:22.622
If he's a Grade 2,
I should be able to handle him.

10:22.705 --> 10:24.206
If he's a Cursed Spirit, that is.

10:24.290 --> 10:25.124
What?

10:26.167 --> 10:28.836
Fushiguro should have said this before.

10:29.337 --> 10:31.297
We usually dispatch a Jujutsu Sorcerer

10:31.380 --> 10:34.091
of the same grade
as the Cursed Spirit to perform the task.

10:34.925 --> 10:39.430
This means a Grade 2 Jujutsu Sorcerer
can beat Grade 2 Cursed Spirits easily.

10:39.513 --> 10:43.517
A Grade 2 Jujutsu Sorcerer is almost
on par with Grade 1 Cursed Spirits.

10:45.645 --> 10:49.065
Why don't I know
such important information?

10:49.148 --> 10:51.108
Because Mr. Gojo's your teacher!

10:54.612 --> 10:56.530
We'll need to get out of the car here.

11:00.117 --> 11:03.954
I feel like I'm in a charade.
This is lame.

11:12.922 --> 11:16.008
If you're going to come out, do it now.

11:18.135 --> 11:20.763
They may look distorted,
and it's too late to save them,

11:20.846 --> 11:23.599
but it's unpleasant to kill humans.

11:26.352 --> 11:29.480
Wow, I'm glad.

11:30.272 --> 11:33.025
I would be troubled
if Satoru Gojo was here.

11:34.110 --> 11:37.196
But if someone too weak comes,
I can't have my experiment.

11:39.156 --> 11:44.078
I don't like working overtime.
Let's make it quick.

00:11:59.208 --> 00:12:01.377
I'll kill you!

00:12:02.753 --> 00:12:04.171
They feel similar.

00:12:04.255 --> 00:12:06.424
That perfectly flippant attitude

00:12:06.507 --> 00:12:08.843
and the sinister strength behind it.

00:12:28.404 --> 00:12:29.238
What?

00:12:31.407 --> 00:12:32.241
What?

00:12:32.867 --> 00:12:35.619
I should've blocked it with cursed energy.

00:12:36.328 --> 00:12:37.997
Is it that kind of cursed technique?

00:12:38.581 --> 00:12:40.207
What do you mean by "that kind"?

00:12:40.291 --> 00:12:44.253
I hate open-ended questions that are
directly thrown at the other party.

00:12:44.336 --> 00:12:45.921
That's great.

00:12:46.005 --> 00:12:48.757
You don't dislike talking.

00:12:48.841 --> 00:12:50.634
It depends on the opponent.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:54.013
A Cursed Spirit
that can communicate this well…

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.016
Mr. Gojo's report only mentioned

00:12:57.099 --> 00:12:59.393
two unregistered
Special Grade Curse Spirits.

00:12:59.477 --> 00:13:02.521
It's hard to believe that
there's no connection between the two.

00:13:04.356 --> 00:13:09.862
Hey, which one do you think came first?
The soul or the body?

00:13:09.945 --> 00:13:10.779
What?

00:13:11.363 --> 00:13:17.786
Isn't there a similar question?
Did the chicken or the egg come first?

00:13:19.705 --> 00:13:22.041
Is the soul hosted in the body?

00:13:22.541 --> 00:13:26.337
Or is the soul enveloping the body?

00:13:27.755 --> 00:13:30.382
I guess I have to hear him out.

00:13:31.675 --> 00:13:32.801
The former.

00:13:32.885 --> 00:13:35.804
Wrong, the latter is the answer.

00:13:37.681 --> 00:13:40.893
The soul always comes before the body.

00:13:41.519 --> 00:13:45.606
The shape of the body is affected
by the shape of the soul.

00:13:46.857 --> 00:13:48.317
I'm not healing myself.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.779
I'm just preserving
the shape of my soul consciously.

00:13:54.406 --> 00:13:56.242
You should understand, right?

00:13:56.325 --> 00:14:00.996
My cursed technique is to touch
the soul and change its shape.

00:14:02.498 --> 00:14:04.416
Idle Transfiguration.

00:14:08.629 --> 00:14:10.631
I store human beings.

00:14:11.131 --> 00:14:12.758
It's quite hard to do that.

00:14:14.051 --> 00:14:18.013
Usually, a person will die
soon after their shape is changed.

00:14:18.889 --> 00:14:20.766
But what about a Jujutsu Sorcerer?

00:14:23.519 --> 00:14:25.062
It's 5:30 p.m. now.

00:14:25.145 --> 00:14:28.107
I started working at 10:00 a.m. today.

00:14:28.607 --> 00:14:32.611
No matter what,
I must get off work by 6:00 p.m.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:41.203
Yoshino.

00:14:41.287 --> 00:14:43.080
Where have you been?

00:14:44.874 --> 00:14:47.793
It's not good to skip school.

00:14:48.377 --> 00:14:50.838
Mr. Sotomura.

00:14:52.006 --> 00:14:53.257
Have you heard?

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:56.844
Sayama, Nishimura, and Honda are dead.

00:14:56.927 --> 00:14:59.680
You're close with them, aren't you?

00:14:59.763 --> 00:15:00.931
What?

00:15:03.392 --> 00:15:05.102
You have no friends.

00:15:05.185 --> 00:15:07.187
They often look after you, don't they?

00:15:07.271 --> 00:15:10.441
But you didn't attend their funeral.

00:15:10.524 --> 00:15:13.110
-You shouldn't be like this.
-Close?

00:15:13.193 --> 00:15:14.570
-Me…
-I'll go with you.

00:15:14.653 --> 00:15:16.447
-…and them?
-At least pay your respects.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:18.657
-He's crazy.
-Okay?

00:15:19.658 --> 00:15:24.496
Teachers work in school
after graduating from one.

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:30.628
You've never experienced
society before, have you?

00:15:30.711 --> 00:15:35.758
That's why there are
giant babies like you!

00:15:37.009 --> 00:15:38.802
Come, open your mouth.

00:15:39.386 --> 00:15:43.265
-Every single one of you…
-Look here.

00:15:45.351 --> 00:15:48.812
I acknowledge
your entire existence, Junpei.

00:15:51.649 --> 00:15:54.485
What are you muttering?

00:15:54.568 --> 00:15:57.655
Did you lose your mind
from staying home? Just joking.

00:16:06.372 --> 00:16:07.206
What?

00:16:09.124 --> 00:16:10.918
This guy…

00:16:11.627 --> 00:16:13.128
He can see it.

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:21.845
It hurts. That guy…

00:16:21.929 --> 00:16:23.347
Take a peek.

00:16:23.847 --> 00:16:25.516
We're starting, Itadori.

00:16:25.599 --> 00:16:27.351
Wait! Someone's coming!

00:16:27.434 --> 00:16:28.268
What?

00:16:28.352 --> 00:16:29.395
Oh, no!

00:16:30.312 --> 00:16:32.481
I'm so glad.

00:16:33.065 --> 00:16:35.484
What's this? Are you a gymnast?

00:16:36.068 --> 00:16:40.239
Hey. I have something to ask you,
so come with me.

00:16:40.322 --> 00:16:42.491
Well…

00:16:42.574 --> 00:16:43.826
Listen to me.

00:16:43.909 --> 00:16:45.244
-This button…
-Wait!

00:16:45.327 --> 00:16:48.747
I'm talking with him. You're so rude.

00:16:48.831 --> 00:16:52.626
Well, this is quite important.

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:54.003
Something important?

00:16:54.086 --> 00:16:55.754
What nonsense are you talking about?

00:16:55.838 --> 00:16:58.257
-Which school are you--
-I pull!

00:16:59.466 --> 00:17:01.844
-What…
-What?

00:17:01.927 --> 00:17:06.306
What are you doing? You brat! Stop it!

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.268
Don't take my pants!

00:17:10.936 --> 00:17:11.979
Stop…

00:17:12.521 --> 00:17:14.440
Stop right there!

00:17:17.818 --> 00:17:19.653
What happened?

00:17:20.571 --> 00:17:21.447
What?

00:17:22.031 --> 00:17:23.490
Well then, let's go.

00:17:23.574 --> 00:17:26.035
That was quick! Have you finished a lap?

00:17:26.118 --> 00:17:26.952
Yes.

00:17:27.036 --> 00:17:29.913
You didn't have to do that.

00:17:29.997 --> 00:17:32.541
You could have just dragged me away.

00:17:32.624 --> 00:17:34.251
Well…

00:17:34.334 --> 00:17:37.087
-But you hate him, right?
-What?

00:17:37.671 --> 00:17:39.840
-Why?
-What?

00:17:39.923 --> 00:17:41.467
Just a feeling.

00:17:41.550 --> 00:17:43.260
Was I wrong?

00:17:43.343 --> 00:17:44.845
It's true.

00:17:45.429 --> 00:17:49.058
You wouldn't want people you hate
to stand in front of your house, right?

00:17:49.725 --> 00:17:51.685
Anyway, let's go over there.

00:17:55.856 --> 00:17:57.107
Okay.

00:18:09.411 --> 00:18:11.163
You're nimble.

00:18:25.094 --> 00:18:26.011
This is fun.

00:18:26.804 --> 00:18:31.475
He changes the form of humans,
but the mass remains the same?

00:18:33.268 --> 00:18:37.689
In any case,
it's not compatible with my technique.

00:18:37.773 --> 00:18:39.983
-Help…
-What?

00:18:40.067 --> 00:18:42.986
Help me.

00:18:45.989 --> 00:18:49.326
A transfigured human can't be saved.

00:18:49.409 --> 00:18:51.829
If you're being attacked,
don't hesitate to kill them.

00:18:51.912 --> 00:18:54.039
This is for the sake of the victims too.

00:18:56.792 --> 00:18:58.752
Oh, sorry.

00:18:59.503 --> 00:19:01.839
I practiced it many times.

00:19:01.922 --> 00:19:04.883
Disfiguration will not
kill them instantly,

00:19:04.967 --> 00:19:09.638
but the accuracy of the brain
or consciousness isn't good enough.

00:19:09.721 --> 00:19:13.100
Sometimes, sweat from the soul
will ooze out like this.

00:19:13.183 --> 00:19:15.102
Don't mind it. Let's continue.

00:19:16.061 --> 00:19:18.397
I don't mind at all.

00:19:21.316 --> 00:19:24.653
I always keep my work
and emotions separate.

00:19:26.405 --> 00:19:30.409
You're bad at lying!
Your soul is wavering.

00:19:30.492 --> 00:19:33.787
Let's see. What grade are you?

00:19:33.871 --> 00:19:35.122
Grade 1.

00:19:35.205 --> 00:19:36.707
No wonder you're strong.

00:19:37.207 --> 00:19:39.960
Your body is perfect for experimentation.

00:19:40.669 --> 00:19:42.504
I'm so lucky.

00:19:44.089 --> 00:19:45.215
Thank you.

00:19:51.471 --> 00:19:54.224
Did the sudden speed increase scare you?

00:19:54.725 --> 00:19:57.853
I can reshape my own soul, too.

00:19:58.979 --> 00:20:02.107
A Jujutsu Sorcerer may have used
cursed energy to protect their body,

00:20:02.191 --> 00:20:04.943
but they have never tried
to protect their soul with it.

00:20:05.027 --> 00:20:08.197
Because to do so, you need
to be conscious of your soul first.

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:10.407
Otherwise, you can't protect it.

00:20:11.033 --> 00:20:15.162
But it seems like you're subconsciously
guarding your soul with cursed energy.

00:20:15.871 --> 00:20:18.916
Otherwise, you'll be my pawn now.

00:20:19.499 --> 00:20:22.628
But if I strike your soul
a few more times,

00:20:22.711 --> 00:20:24.546
you won't be a human anymore!

00:20:33.597 --> 00:20:34.973
I won't let you escape!

00:20:49.404 --> 00:20:52.407
Is that all, Grade 1 Jujutsu Sorcerer?

00:20:52.491 --> 00:20:54.159
You tried so hard to escape.

00:20:54.243 --> 00:20:56.286
But you should be
reaching your limits, right?

00:21:03.126 --> 00:21:04.878
Unfortunately…

00:21:06.755 --> 00:21:08.173
What's this?

00:21:08.674 --> 00:21:11.510
His cursed energy is rising.

00:21:11.593 --> 00:21:15.555
I'll start working overtime.

00:22:46.646 --> 00:22:48.482
-Juju Stroll!
-Juju Stroll!

00:22:49.066 --> 00:22:50.484
Fushiguro!

00:22:50.567 --> 00:22:52.652
Did you see my uniform jacket?

00:22:52.736 --> 00:22:54.071
No, I didn't see it.

00:22:54.154 --> 00:22:57.741
That's strange. I thought I left it here.

00:22:57.824 --> 00:22:58.784
Hey.

00:22:58.867 --> 00:23:01.745
Panda, did you see my uniform jacket?

00:23:02.329 --> 00:23:03.580
What?

00:23:03.663 --> 00:23:06.249
I didn't see it.

00:23:06.833 --> 00:23:10.754
Is that so? I wonder where it went!

00:23:14.966 --> 00:23:17.427
Hey, my skirt's missing too.

00:23:17.511 --> 00:23:20.263
This is the bottom line
that can't be crossed!

00:23:22.599 --> 00:23:23.600
Mustard!

00:23:24.101 --> 00:23:25.268
Bonito flakes…

00:23:27.604 --> 00:23:29.773
This bunch of trash!

00:23:30.649 --> 00:23:32.400
What a scene to behold.

00:23:33.610 --> 00:23:34.653
What?

00:23:35.362 --> 00:23:37.280
This is Maki's.

00:23:38.949 --> 00:23:40.408
Good evening!

00:23:40.492 --> 00:23:43.078
I'm Nobara Kugisaki!
